Layout ideas mapped to platformer levels:# Interface Vision# Interface Vision

Sidequest Mail should feel like a retro platformer — but work like Proton Mail.
The pixel art is the skin, not the mechanics.
Everything below is aesthetic and optional; the core email flow (read, reply, file, delete) must always be instant.

---

## Layout Grid

| Screen       | Platformer Concept           | Behavior                                                                 |
|:-------------|:-----------------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Inbox**    | Level 1: The Start           | Emails sit on platforms like blocks. Unread emails glow or pulse.        |
|              |                              | Reading one "collects" it — it moves to the Read section.                |
| **Folders**  | Checkpoints                  | Each folder is a checkpoint you teleport to.                             |
|              |                              | Navigating there shows: *"Checkpoint accepted!"*                         |
| **Sent**     | The Finish Line              | You reached the end. "Level Complete" energy.                            |
| **Trash**    | The Pit                      | Where things fall. Dragging an email there drops it into the abyss.      |
|              |                              | Restoring it is "grabbing it mid-fall."                                  |
| **Drafts**   | The Build Area               | Still under construction. Incomplete bricks, half-formed structures.     |

